**App name** (30 characters or fewer)
DropLink: Share Files Anywhere

**Short description** (80 characters or fewer)
Share files, music and video from your phone to any browser. No cloud, no cable.

You could also use: "Turn your phone into a private file server for Windows, Mac, Linux and iPhone."

**Full description** (3,984 characters; the limit is 4,000)

DropLink turns your Android phone into a private file server and media player for your own network. Open your music, videos, photos and documents on any other device (Windows PC, Mac, Linux, iPhone, iPad, Chromebook, another Android phone or a smart TV) straight from its web browser. Nothing to install on the other device, no cloud, no account, no cable.

HOW IT WORKS
1. Pick the folders you want to share.
2. Tap Start hosting.
3. On the other device, scan the QR code or open the address shown on your phone.
4. Approve the new device on your phone. That's it.

SHARE WITH ANY DEVICE
• Works on Android, iOS and iPadOS, Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS and more: if it has a modern browser, it can connect.
• Browse your shared folders, preview photos, PDFs and text, and download anything with one tap. Folders open quickly, with small thumbnails instead of full photos.
• Interrupted downloads and uploads pick up where they stopped.
• Only your phone needs the app. Everyone else just uses a browser.

SEND FILES BOTH WAYS
• Connected devices can send files to your phone, but only after you approve: once, or always for a device you trust. You can set each device to Ask, Always or Block.
• Send files from your phone to one device or everyone online. They appear under "From the phone" with a notice.
• See per-file progress both ways. Received files are saved in Downloads/DropLink and open in other apps with a tap.
• Phone to phone: pair two phones with DropLink and send files straight between them. It is fast, resumes if stopped, and the other owner still approves.

A PLAYER THAT KEEPS PLAYING
• A built-in music and video player with Recent, Music, Videos and Favorites, an editable queue, shuffle, repeat, speed control and a sleep timer.
• Videos continue where you left off, with subtitles (srt, vtt, ass). Songs show synced lyrics that follow the music.
• Plays in the background with notification and lock-screen controls.
• Live streaming (optional, off each time the app starts): connected devices follow your phone's player in their browser, with the queue, lyrics and subtitles.
• In the browser, songs and videos open in a full player page with lists from their own folder (All, Music, Videos, Recent).

YOU STAY IN CONTROL
• Folders are shared read-only. DropLink never copies or uploads them.
• Every new device must be approved on your phone. See who is online in the Devices screen and revoke any device whenever you like.
• Connections are encrypted with HTTPS and stay on your hotspot or Wi-Fi.
• No ads, no analytics, no trackers, no accounts. Your files never touch our servers, because we don't have any.

BUILT FOR EVERYDAY USE
• A clean web client that you can install as an app, with light and dark themes and your choice of accent colour.
• Accessibility: keyboard shortcuts, screen-reader support, larger text, high contrast, reduced motion.
• Camera Nodes: turn a spare phone, tablet or laptop into a live camera, or a sound-only monitor. You allow each device. Others watch several cameras at once, talk back, take snapshots, record moments, switch its flashlight and get motion alerts. The video goes straight between browsers, not through your phone.
• Optional: host a small website from your phone, with sign-in accounts and forms that send information to your phone.
• Meet Aubree, the friendly mascot who guides you through each step.

FREE AND OPEN SOURCE
DropLink is free and open source under the Apache 2.0 licence. Read the code, report an issue or suggest an idea on GitHub: github.com/trebronwayne/DropLink

GOOD TO KNOW
• Your phone and the other device must be on the same network, for example your phone's hotspot or the same Wi-Fi.
• Because the connection is encrypted with a certificate made on your phone, a browser may ask you to trust it the first time you connect.
• Keep Battery Saver off while hosting so Android doesn't pause DropLink.
• Requires Android 8.0 or newer.

